# Force LF line endings on checkout regardless of the checkout machine's `core.autocrlf` (issue
# #111): Windows runners (GitHub Actions windows-latest, and Git for Windows locally) default
# core.autocrlf=true, which converts every text file's stored LF endings to CRLF on checkout. That
# broke apps/daemon/test/docs-claim-check.test.mjs and preflight.test.mjs -- Vitest's SSR module
# loader throws "SyntaxError: Invalid or unexpected token" when dynamically importing a CRLF-ended
# .mjs file (scripts/docs-claim-check.mjs, scripts/preflight.mjs), even though Node's own parser
# and esbuild's own transform() both parse the identical CRLF content without error. `eol=lf` here
# pins the working-tree line ending independent of any user's or runner's autocrlf setting.
* text=auto eol=lf
